16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">The new item can also be added by clicking on’ Add New Item’.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">Once all the details are filled and the total of Debit and Credit are equal you may save it.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">On saving, trial balance will be added to the list on the main page.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><br style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><strong style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">QuickBooks Online Import</span></strong></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">You can directly import a Trial Balance from QuickBooks Online. Upon importing those entries, you will need to map the Trial Balance according to Capium's Chart of Accounts</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><br style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"><strong dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">Xero Import&nbsp;</strong><br style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"></span></span></span></p><p style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">You can directly import a Trial Balance from Xero. Upon importing those entries, you will need to map the Trial Balance according to Capium's Chart of Accounts</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><br style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Helvetica Neue;\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-size: 16px;\">Related Articles</span></strong></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p><a dir=\"ltr\" href=\"https://support.capium.com/support/solutions/articles/9000186950-how-to-prepare-a-set-of-accounts\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Click here for a walkthrough on how to prepare a 